module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Eval
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RegularLocalRing.Defs
public import Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
public import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.GRing

/-! # Regularity of the polynomial parameter map over a prime field

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07DY; More on Algebra, Tags 07PS, 07PV,
0H7U and 07C0 (blueprint: lem-per-prime-field-parameter-regular-map).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- Evaluation at a regular system of parameters is regular over a prime field.
No completeness of the target is needed.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07DY; More on Algebra, Tags 07PS, 07PV,
0H7U and 07C0 (blueprint: lem-per-prime-field-parameter-regular-map).

Proof: Let P be the polynomial ring, m its variable ideal, and A=P_m. The origin
localization is regular local of dimension d, with maximal ideal generated by the
variables (Tag 00OP). The inverse image of the maximal ideal of B is m: the
parameters lie in that maximal ideal, and m is maximal since P/m=k. Thus evaluation
extends to a local map A→B. A generating list of length dim B is regular in B
(Tag 00NQ), so Tag 07DY makes A→B flat. Its closed fibre is F=B/n, over k=A/mA.
The field k is complete at its zero ideal and hence a G-ring (07PS); its finite-type
algebra P is a G-ring (07PV), so the completion map of A is regular. Every finite
purely inseparable extension of the prime field k is trivial: in characteristic
zero this follows from separability, and in characteristic p the Frobenius of
F_p is bijective. Hence F/k is geometrically regular, as each tested base change
is isomorphic to the regular Noetherian field F. The local closed-fibre criterion
0H7U gives regularity of A→B. B has only one maximal ideal; its localization there
is B itself and its contraction to P is m. The maximal-local criterion 07C0 now
gives regularity of P→B. For d=0, A=k and B is a field, and the same argument applies.
-/
theorem prime_field_parameter_map_isRegular
    (k B : Type u) [Field k] [CommRing B] [Algebra k B]
    (hprime : Nonempty (k ≃+* ℚ) ∨
      ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ Nonempty (k ≃+* ZMod p))
    [IsRegularLocalRing B] (d : ℕ)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim B = (d : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (t : Fin d → B) (hgen : Ideal.span (Set.range t) = maximalIdeal B) :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := k) t).toRingHom.IsRegular := by sorry

end IsLocalRing
